cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "boutscope: ground truth for behavioural categorisers"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "0.4.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zerotonin/boutscope"
keywords:
  - behaviour
  - ethology
  - pose-estimation
  - annotation
  - ground-truth
  - keypoint-MoSeq
  - clustering
  - Python
authors:
  - given-names: "Bart R.H."
    family-names: Geurten
    email: bart.geurten@otago.ac.nz
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1816-3241"
    affiliation: "Department of Zoology, University of Otago, Dunedin, New Zealand"
abstract: >-
  boutscope collects ground truth for the output of behavioural
  categorisers such as k-means prototype movements, keypoint-MoSeq
  syllables, B-SOiD, VAME or SimBA.  Adapters turn a categoriser's
  per-frame labels into one project format; boutscope indexes the
  labels into bouts, draws seeded and stratified samples of bouts in
  a chosen duration range, shows them in the original video and
  records verdicts, from which it estimates the precision of every
  label with a confidence interval.
